<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-nicaragua"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Nicaragua.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Nicaragua</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Sandinista revolution overthrows Anastasio Somoza Debayle</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/south-yemen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20Yemen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South Yemen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Border war with North Yemen; treaty of friendship with the Soviet Union</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Arab%20Emirates.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Arab Emirates</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jebel Ali port opens; Rashid of Dubai becomes prime minister</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">China attacks across the northern border in the Sino-Vietnamese War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/uganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Uganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Uganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tanzanian forces and Ugandan exiles take Kampala and overthrow Amin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tanzania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tanzania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tanzania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tanzanian forces capture Kampala and overthrow Idi Amin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/theocracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Theocracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Theocracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A revolution and a new constitution make Iran an Islamic Republic headed by a senior Shia jurist</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/sami"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/S%C3%A1mi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sámi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Alta hydro-electric controversy brings Sámi rights onto the political agenda</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/saudi-arabia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saudi%20Arabia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saudi Arabia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Iranian Revolution and the seizure of the Grand Mosque in Mecca by Islamist militants, retaken after ten days, push the royal family towards stricter religious observance and a greater role for the ulema.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-egypt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Egypt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Egypt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Egypt–Israel peace treaty is signed after Sadat's 1977 visit to Jerusalem; Egypt is temporarily expelled from the Arab League.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 1 June under the Internal Settlement Abel Muzorewa becomes the first black prime minister of the renamed Zimbabwe Rhodesia; the Lancaster House Agreement ends UDI in December.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/inuit"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Inuit.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Inuit</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Denmark grants Greenland home rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/bon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Central Tibetan Administration in exile accepts Bon as a religious group with the same rights as the Buddhist schools</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/solidarity"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Solidarity.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Solidarity</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Pope John Paul II visits Poland, a visit Lech Wałęsa later called a significant factor in the creation of Solidarity</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/non-aligned-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Non-Aligned%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Non-Aligned Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Fidel Castro chairs the Havana summit; months later the movement is split by the Soviet intervention in Afghanistan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/capitalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Capitalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Capitalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Margaret Thatcher takes office in Britain, and with Ronald Reagan’s presidency from 1981 monetarism gains prominence across the capitalist world</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A revolution led by Ayatollah Ruhollah Khomeini overthrows the Shah and creates the Islamic Republic of Iran</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">An armed fundamentalist group seizes the Grand Mosque in Mecca and holds it for over a week</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/lascaux"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lascaux.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lascaux</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lascaux is inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List as part of the Prehistoric Sites and Decorated Caves of the Vézère Valley</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/florentine-codex"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Florentine%20Codex.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Florentine Codex</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Mexican government publishes a full-colour three-volume facsimile in a limited edition of 2,000</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/moai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Moai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Moai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sergio Rapu Haoa and a team of archaeologists showed that the eye sockets had held coral eyes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/karnak"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Karnak.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Karnak</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Karnak was added to the UNESCO World Heritage List along with the rest of the city of Thebes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/neoliberalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Neoliberalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Neoliberalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Margaret Thatcher becomes Conservative prime minister, a post she holds until 1990</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Iranian Revolution ousts Shah Mohammad Reza Pahlavi</span></li></ul></section>
